WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.279 --> 00:00:02.112
(light music)

00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:03.070
- [Narrator] While it
looks like tree bark,

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.380
there is more here than meets the eye.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.636
This is Madagascar's
mossy leaf-tailed gecko.

00:00:09.636 --> 00:00:12.136
(light music)

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.110
There are few animals in
the world that exhibit

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.080
such incredible camouflage as a

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.713
mossy leaf-tailed gecko.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.510
Growing up to six inches in length,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.800
their bodies are lined
with small flaps of skin

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.780
that help scatter their shadows,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.380
making their outline nearly
invisible to predators.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.530
Endemic to Madagascar, these
geckos spend their lives

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.256
on the trunks and branches
of dense rainforest fauna.

00:00:38.256 --> 00:00:40.060
Nocturnal in nature, they use their

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.960
elliptical shaped pupils
to hunt for insects

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.480
and small invertebrates
in the dead of night.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.810
In spite of their formidable camouflage,

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.690
the mossy leaf tailed gecko's future

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.770
is threatened due to deforestation

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.480
and increasing demand in the pet trade.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.232
This is the mossy leaf-tailed gecko.

00:00:57.232 --> 00:00:59.732
(light music)

